Taken: ManagedShell.Interop, ManagedShell.Common (without search, startup and the shell window), ManagedShell.WindowsTray,
ManagedShell.WindowsTasks, ManagedShell.UWPInterop and the ExplorerHelper and AppBarManager of ManagedShell.AppBar.

Changed for HeMiDock (2026-11-04): no WPF and no Windows Forms – pictures of icons are pixels (ShellImage) read by calls
of Windows, the WPF dispatcher and timer are replaced by ShellDispatcher and ShellTimer, the message window of Windows
Forms by an own one (Compat.cs), collections are plain ObservableCollections instead of WPF views and dependency
properties, the AppBarManager only answers the AppBar messages (no AppBar windows), the icons of Store apps come from
the shell through HeMiDock, and ShellManager only starts what HeMiDock uses.

Arranged for HeMiDock (2026-11-05): the files of each area are joined into one file (AppBar, Common, Helpers, Logging,
Interop, Uwp, AppWindows, Tray); the name of every original file stays as a heading inside.